<v Ira Glass>Act Four, The Girl With the Golden Gloves. So now we travel back in time to a sweaty gym in 1998. That's when this was first broadcast. It's about somebody with a complicated relationship with the sport she loves from Meema Spadola.
<v Ira Glass>第四幕，拥有金手套的女孩。所以现在我们回到1998年的一家汗流浃背的健身房。那是这个第一次播出的时候。这是关于一个与她热爱的运动有复杂关系的人，来自米玛·斯帕多拉。

00:48:32.910 --> 00:48:46.680
<v Meema Spadola>Maritza was an accountant, a financial analyst at a huge insurance company. She was living day-to-day like anybody else. Then she heard about this boxing class that was being offered at the company gym. Some guy named Milton was teaching.
<v Meema Spadola>玛丽扎是一名会计师，一家大型保险公司的财务分析师。她像其他人一样过着日子。然后她听说公司健身房正在提供这种拳击课程。一个叫米尔顿的家伙在教。

00:48:46.680 --> 00:48:53.220
<v Meema Spadola>Maritza liked sports. She'd even taken an aerobic boxing class before. So she decided to go down and check it out.
<v Meema Spadola>玛丽扎喜欢体育。她甚至以前参加过有氧拳击课程。所以她决定去看看。

00:48:53.220 --> 00:49:00.150
<v Maritza Arroyo>Here I am in a suit, coming in. It was the first time. I didn't have a chance to change. So I'm walking in all suited up.
<v Maritza Arroyo>我穿着西装，进来了。这是第一次。我没机会换衣服。所以我穿着全套西装走进来。

00:49:00.150 --> 00:49:07.590
<v Milton>So Maritza comes up, and she's so short. She goes, I want to get rid of my stomach. I want to get rid of my gut.
<v Milton>所以玛丽扎来了，她太矮了。她说，我想摆脱我的肚子。我想摆脱我的肥肉。

00:49:07.590 --> 00:49:20.320
<v Milton>She was so short. I look at her. And I go, honey, I teach boxing. This ain't boxing aerobics, aero boxing. If you want to come and dance around, jump around, I said, I'm not the guy for you. So this ain't what you want.
<v Milton>她太矮了。我看着她。我说，亲爱的，我教拳击。这不是拳击有氧，有氧拳击。如果你想来跳舞，跳来跳去，我说，我不是你要找的人。所以这不是你要的。

00:49:20.320 --> 00:49:33.210
<v Maritza Arroyo>He wasn't even thinking about me. There's another girl who thinks this is aero-- I mean-- so I threw a punch. He goes, oh, you got a pretty good punch there. He goes, let me see what you got. Bam, bam.
<v Maritza Arroyo>他甚至没考虑我。还有另一个女孩以为这是有氧——我的意思是——所以我打了一拳。他去，噢，你那拳打得不错。他去，让我看看你有什么。砰，砰。

00:49:33.210 --> 00:49:38.460
<v Maritza Arroyo>You got a pretty good punch there, he goes. But who taught you how to box? Two steps. Then he's, like, trying to fix me.
<v Maritza Arroyo>你打了一拳不错，他说。但谁教你怎么打拳？两步。然后他，就像，试图修理我。

00:49:38.460 --> 00:49:49.830
<v Maritza Arroyo>I'm going to teach you how to weave. I'm going to shine you up like an old shoe and polish you up. He made me laugh. I thought it was amusing. I found it amusing.
<v Maritza Arroyo>我要教你怎么编织。我要像擦旧鞋一样把你擦亮，把你打磨好。他让我笑了。我觉得这很有趣。我觉得这很有趣。

00:49:49.830 --> 00:49:57.270
<v Maritza Arroyo>It reminded me of watching the old movies. And this guy's telling me I'm like an old shoe. He's going to polish me. This guy's got an act.
<v Maritza Arroyo>这让我想起了看老电影。这家伙告诉我我像一只旧鞋子。他要擦亮我。这家伙有一套表演。

00:49:57.270 --> 00:50:06.810
<v Milton>So I started working with her every day, come down with the pads, giving her combinations. And she started falling into place. So I was like, whoa.
<v Milton>所以我开始每天和她一起工作，带着垫子下来，给她组合拳。她开始就位。所以我就像，哇。

00:50:06.810 --> 00:50:20.730
<v Milton>I said, you know something? I said, if I could bring you to my gym in Brooklyn, I said, you could win the New York City Golden Gloves. She goes, I can? I go, honey, what I got you doing right now, no girl fights the way you do right now.
<v Milton>我说，你知道吗？我说，如果我能带你去我在布鲁克林的健身房，我说，你可以赢得纽约市金手套奖。她去，我可以？我去，亲爱的，我现在让你做的，没有女孩像你这样打架。

00:50:20.730 --> 00:50:24.250
<v Maritza Arroyo>So that's how it all started.
<v Maritza Arroyo>所以这就是一切开始的方式。

00:50:24.250 --> 00:50:46.360
<v Meema Spadola>Every day after work in Manhattan, Maritza would take the subway all the way out to Brooklyn to train for three or four hours at Milton's gym and then go all the way back home to Queens. She spent her weekends at the gym. No one in her old life understood what she was doing. She'd grown up in the projects, put herself through college, gotten an MBA, held a good paying job, and here she was, back so close to the streets.
<v Meema Spadola>曼哈顿下班后，玛丽扎每天都会乘地铁一直到布鲁克林，在米尔顿的健身房训练三四个小时，然后一直回家到皇后区。她周末在健身房度过。她过去生活中的没人明白她在做什么。她在项目中长大，通过大学，获得MBA，拥有一份高薪工作，而这里她，回到了离街道如此近的地方。

00:50:46.360 --> 00:51:12.980
<v Meema Spadola>When she got a broken nose and black eyes in the ring, she lied to her coworkers about it, didn't tell them she was boxing. Her parents didn't approve of women fighting. They were conservative, born in Puerto Rico. Her friends were suspicious of her weight loss. They accused her of being anorexic, infected with HIV, or addicted to drugs. But at the gym, everyone believed in her. Maritza was the only girl at Milton's, his first girl. So she'd spar with the men there.
<v Meema Spadola>当她在拳击场上折断鼻子并有黑眼圈时，她对同事撒谎，没告诉他们她在打拳。她的父母不赞成女性打架。他们是保守的，出生在波多黎各。她的朋友对她的体重减轻感到怀疑。他们指责她患有厌食症，感染HIV，或吸毒。但在健身房，每个人都相信她。玛丽扎是米尔顿唯一的女孩，他的第一个女孩。所以她会和那里的男人陪练。

00:51:12.980 --> 00:51:32.690
<v Milton>She took Joey one day, and she was throwing nonstop combinations and punches repetitiously. There was an old man sitting down in a chair, and he goes, god damn, that boy can throw some punches. She had the head gear on. So when she finished, he came over and he goes, that's going to be one good damn fighter. That boy is going to be great.
<v Milton>她有一天带了乔伊，她重复地扔着不间断的组合拳。有个老人坐在椅子上，他去，该死，那男孩能扔几拳。她戴着头盔。所以当她完成时，他走过来他去，那将是一个不错的斗士。那男孩会很棒。

00:51:32.690 --> 00:51:40.060
<v Milton>I go, I hate to tell you this. That's no guy. He goes, what do you mean that's no guy? Looked like a guy. I go, that's a girl. He goes, get out of here.
<v Milton>我去，我不愿告诉你这个。那不是家伙。他去，你什么意思那不是家伙？看起来像个家伙。我去，那是女孩。他去，离开这里。

00:51:40.060 --> 00:51:56.270
<v Milton>So I said, Maritza, come here. So she came over to me, and I took off her head gear. I go, does she look like a girl now? He goes, oh.
<v Milton>所以我说，玛丽扎，过来。所以她走到我身边，我摘下了她的头盔。我去，她现在看起来像女孩吗？他去，噢。

00:51:56.270 --> 00:52:13.550
<v Meema Spadola>Looking at Maritza, you probably wouldn't think boxer. She's small, just over 5 feet tall, and only 106 pounds. Her features are fine and delicate. But when she talks about her love for boxing, you can see her in the ring. She's radiant. It's like speaking to someone who's had a religious conversion.
<v Meema Spadola>看着玛丽扎，你可能不会想到拳击手。她很小，刚超过5英尺高，只有106磅。她的特征细腻而精致。但当她谈论她对拳击的热爱时，你可以看到她在拳击场。她容光焕发。这就像和一个经历过宗教皈依的人说话。

00:52:13.550 --> 00:52:28.660
<v Maritza Arroyo>Boxing has shed a light on me. It's like my vision. It's like I just obtained a vision. It's like-- this is what I was put here for.
<v Maritza Arroyo>拳击照亮了我。这就像我的愿景。这就像我刚刚获得了一个愿景。这就像——这是我被放在这里的原因。

00:52:28.660 --> 00:52:44.580
<v Announcer>Ladies and gentlemen, tonight's next bout is the women's 106 pound class. The referee is Pete Santiago. In the gold corner, Maritza Arroyo from the Supreme Team Boxing Club. Arroyo is a financial analyst and a part-time personal trainer.
<v Announcer>女士们，先生们，今晚的下一场比赛是女子106磅级。裁判是皮特·圣地亚哥。在金角落，来自Supreme Team Boxing Club的玛丽扎·阿罗约。阿罗约是一名财务分析师和兼职私人教练。

00:52:44.580 --> 00:53:03.100
<v Meema Spadola>With Milton's training, Maritza was unbeatable. Within a year, she had taken all the amateur titles in New York. She won the Metros, the Empire States, and in '96 she won the biggest of all, the Golden Gloves in Madison Square Garden, a fight televised around the world, held in a ring where some of the greatest boxers in history have fought.
<v Meema Spadola>在米尔顿的训练下，玛丽扎是不可战胜的。一年之内，她拿下了纽约所有的业余冠军头衔。她赢得了大都会，帝国之州，在96年她赢得了最大的奖项，麦迪逊广场花园的金手套奖，一场向世界转播的比赛，在一个历史上最伟大的拳击手曾战斗过的拳击场举行。

00:53:03.100 --> 00:53:12.230
<v Announcer>Two straight left hands by Arroyo. And another straight left. Four straight left hands by Arroyo.
<v Announcer>阿罗约的两记直左拳。还有一记直左拳。阿罗约的四记直左拳。

00:53:12.230 --> 00:53:27.480
<v Meema Spadola>Maritza and I get together to watch the video of her '96 Golden Gloves win. The garden's packed. The crowd's going wild. Maritza's incredibly fast and beautiful in the ring. Watching her, you understand what it means to be a smart fighter. She's calculated.
<v Meema Spadola>玛丽扎和我聚在一起观看她96年赢得金手套的录像。花园挤满了人。人群疯狂了。玛丽扎在拳击场上难以置信地快速而美丽。看着她，你明白成为一个聪明的斗士意味着什么。她很算计。

00:53:27.480 --> 00:53:43.800
<v Meema Spadola>The woman she's fighting is taller than she is, with longer arms. So Maritza ducks down low and jabs up to the body, choosing where she lands her punches-- to the ribs, then to the chest. And when her opponent can barely catch her breath, Maritza's up, giving her a fierce combination to the face and head.
<v Meema Spadola>她正在战斗的女人比她高，有更长的手臂。所以玛丽扎低头躲避，向身体刺拳，选择她落在哪里——肋骨，然后是胸部。当她的对手几乎喘不过气来时，玛丽扎站了起来，给她的脸和头一记激烈的组合拳。

00:53:43.800 --> 00:53:47.130
<v Maritza Arroyo>There goes the uppercuts. There goes another one to the body.
<v Maritza Arroyo>上勾拳来了。又来了一个身体上的。

00:53:47.130 --> 00:53:48.210
<v Meema Spadola>Ow.
<v Meema Spadola>噢。

00:53:48.210 --> 00:53:51.330
<v Maritza Arroyo>Another one to the body, another one, another one.
<v Maritza Arroyo>又一个身体上的，又一个，又一个。

00:53:51.330 --> 00:54:02.890
<v Meema Spadola>In the last 10 seconds, Manson gets in a good punch, straight to Maritza's face. Maritza stumbles back and then seems to go crazy. She throws nonstop combinations, and the crowd is screaming.
<v Meema Spadola>最后10秒，曼森打出了一记好拳，直击玛丽扎的脸。玛丽扎向后踉跄，然后似乎疯了。她扔出不间断的组合拳，人群在尖叫。

00:54:02.890 --> 00:54:08.570
<v Maritza Arroyo>There, there goes the hook. See that? Whoa. That's it. 10 seconds. Bam. There you go. I threw it all.
<v Maritza Arroyo>那里，勾拳来了。看见了吗？哇。就是这样。10秒。砰。给你。我扔了一切。

00:54:08.570 --> 00:54:16.360
<v Maritza Arroyo>Go, go. There you go. There you go. There you go. There you go. Throw it. I missed a lot, but I threw.
<v Maritza Arroyo>走，走。给你。给你。给你。给你。扔它。我错过了很多，但我扔了。

00:54:16.360 --> 00:54:18.150
<v Maritza Arroyo>[BELL RINGING]
<v Maritza Arroyo>[铃声响起]

00:54:18.150 --> 00:54:29.100
<v Meema Spadola>Can we just watch the last 10 seconds? That was so cool. Oh my god. You are so good, Maritza. I want to see you fight so badly.
<v Meema Spadola>我们可以只看最后10秒吗？那太酷了。天哪。你太棒了，玛丽扎。我太想看你打架了。

00:54:29.100 --> 00:54:35.000
<v Ira Glass>After the fight ends, we're laughing. We keep rewinding to watch Maritza's amazing finale.
<v Ira Glass>比赛结束后，我们在笑。我们一直在倒带看玛丽扎令人惊叹的终曲。

00:54:35.000 --> 00:54:48.620
<v Maritza Arroyo>I'm like, really? You got it good, right? Well, OK. All right, all right, all right, all right. OK, OK. Yeah, that was a grin. That was a good grin. That was a good grin.
<v Maritza Arroyo>我就像，真的？你做得很好，对吗？好吧，好的。好的，好的，好的，好的。好的，好的。是的，那是一个咧嘴笑。那是一个好咧嘴笑。那是一个好咧嘴笑。

00:54:48.620 --> 00:54:59.660
<v Meema Spadola>We're both completely high and hysterical. Maritza's face is transformed. This is pure joy. And in a way it's terrible, because we both know she's quitting boxing.
<v Meema Spadola>我们两个都完全亢奋和歇斯底里。玛丽扎的脸变了。这是纯粹的快乐。从某种意义上说，这太可怕了，因为我们都知道她要退出拳击。

00:54:59.660 --> 00:55:12.800
<v Meema Spadola>Maritza wants to go pro, but there doesn't seem to be any way she could make a living at boxing. She's only 106 pounds. They don't even have a name for her weight class. If she went pro, no one knows of any women who are good enough to match her.
<v Meema Spadola>玛丽扎想走职业，但似乎没有办法能让她通过拳击谋生。她只有106磅。他们甚至没有给她的体重级命名。如果她走职业，没人知道有什么女性好到足以匹配她。

00:55:12.800 --> 00:55:32.990
<v Meema Spadola>As it is, there are only two amateur women at her level. In all her title matches, she's always been put up against these same two opponents over and over. And she's beat them every time. In 10 years, there may be enough women that Maritza would be able to make a career of it, but she's already in her 30s. She says she has to be realistic about the future.
<v Meema Spadola>实际上，在她的水平上只有两个业余女性。在她所有的冠军赛中，她总是被安排与这两个对手一次又一次地对抗。她每次都击败了她们。10年内，可能有足够的女性让玛丽扎能够从事这个职业，但她已经30多岁了。她说她必须对未来现实一点。

00:55:32.990 --> 00:55:48.750
<v Maritza Arroyo>I get mixed feelings. When I go into the gym, I want to do it. But when I come away from the gym and I start looking at reality, it's like, I'm sad. It's like a sadness.
<v Maritza Arroyo>我有复杂的感觉。当我进入健身房，我想做。但当我离开健身房开始面对现实时，就像，我很伤心。这就像一种悲伤。

00:55:48.750 --> 00:55:58.340
<v Maritza Arroyo>Nobody sees it on the outside. No one sees it. But on the inside, it's like it died. It's like, god, it could have been you. You should be in there, boxing.
<v Maritza Arroyo>没人从外面看到它。没人看到它。但在里面，就像它死了。就像，天哪，本来可能是你。你应该在那里面，打拳。

00:55:58.340 --> 00:56:31.010
<v Meema Spadola>It's like she's in love with someone she knows she has to leave. So she circles around boxing, quits, comes back for one-night stands. Last year, Milton signed her up for the Metros tournament without telling her. On the night of the fight, he called her from ringside and told her they were holding up the match for her. Maritza got in her car and drove from Queens to Brooklyn while Milton lied to the judges about Maritza being stuck in traffic. She arrived, beat her opponent in three rounds flat, but was so disgusted with herself for fighting when she was trying to retire that she left without even collecting her trophy.
<v Meema Spadola>就像她爱上了一个她知道必须离开的人。所以她在拳击周围徘徊，退出，回来进行一夜情。去年，米尔顿在没告诉她的情况下给她报名参加了大都会锦标赛。比赛当晚，他从拳击场边打电话给她，说他们在为她推迟比赛。玛丽扎上了她的车，从皇后区开车到布鲁克林，而米尔顿对裁判撒谎说玛丽扎被困在交通中。她到了，在三回合内打败了她的对手，但因为她在试图退休时打架而对自己感到非常厌恶，以至于她没带走她的奖杯就走了。

00:56:31.010 --> 00:56:48.980
<v Meema Spadola>But being back in the game felt too good. And after that win, she just couldn't bring herself to walk away. Despite her reservations, she went on to fight in the 1997 New York Gloves and, of course, won.
<v Meema Spadola>但回到比赛中感觉太好了。而在那次胜利之后，她只是无法让自己离开。尽管有顾虑，她还是继续参加了1997年的纽约金手套比赛，当然，赢了。

00:56:48.980 --> 00:56:52.840
<v Milton>Come right here real quick. There you go. See the difference? Go.
<v Milton>马上过来。给你。看见不同了吗？走。

00:56:52.840 --> 00:57:10.510
<v Meema Spadola>In February, just after Maritza misses the deadline for the 1998 Golden Gloves, I go to Milton's gym to see her fight. Even though, these days, Maritza isn't there much anymore, Milton has promised me that Maritza will spar with a new girl he's training. We wait and wait, and no Maritza. An hour passes.
<v Meema Spadola>二月，就在玛丽扎错过1998年金手套比赛报名截止日期后，我去米尔顿的健身房看她打架。尽管这些天玛丽扎已经不在那里了，米尔顿向我保证玛丽扎会和他在训练的一个新女孩进行陪练。我们等啊等啊，没玛丽扎。一个小时过去了。

00:57:10.510 --> 00:57:19.810
<v Meema Spadola>When she finally shows, she looks worn out and tired. She's not dressed to box, and she says she's got the flu. She's not going to fight. Right away, everyone starts pushing her.
<v Meema Spadola>当她最终出现时，她看起来筋疲力尽。她没穿拳击装，她说她得了流感。她不打算打架。立刻，每个人都开始推她。

00:57:19.810 --> 00:57:20.740
<v Woman>Well, let's just do a little.
<v Woman>好吧，让我们做一点吧。

00:57:20.740 --> 00:57:21.560
<v Maritza Arroyo>Do you want to?
<v Maritza Arroyo>你想要吗？

00:57:21.560 --> 00:57:22.030
<v Woman>Yeah.
<v Woman>是的。

00:57:22.030 --> 00:57:23.340
<v Maritza Arroyo>But I got nothing with me.
<v Maritza Arroyo>但我什么都没带。

00:57:23.340 --> 00:57:24.370
<v Woman>What do you need?
<v Woman>你需要什么？

00:57:24.370 --> 00:57:27.730
<v Maritza Arroyo>Everything. I don't have nothing.
<v Maritza Arroyo>一切。我什么都没有。

00:57:27.730 --> 00:57:37.660
<v Meema Spadola>She says she didn't bring her shoes. She doesn't have any of her gear. Milton points to some shoes lying in the corner, says they're her size. Suddenly, Maritza doesn't look so tired.
<v Meema Spadola>她说她没带她的鞋。她没有任何装备。米尔顿指着角落里放着的几双鞋，说它们是她的尺码。突然，玛丽扎看起来没那么累了。

00:57:37.660 --> 00:57:40.240
<v Maritza Arroyo>But I got to tell you, I have no mouthpiece.
<v Maritza Arroyo>但我得告诉你，我没带牙套。

00:57:40.240 --> 00:57:51.970
<v Meema Spadola>Then Maritza drops the pretense. We head down in the elevator to her car. Turns out, she's been carrying her gloves, her mouthpiece, her wraps, all of her equipment in her car for the past year, just in case.
<v Meema Spadola>然后玛丽扎放弃了假装。我们乘电梯去她的车。原来，过去一年她一直把她的手套、牙套、绷带，所有装备放在车里，以防万一。

00:57:51.970 --> 00:57:55.270
<v Maritza Arroyo>I knew this was going to happen. That's why I don't want to come around here. That's why I don't want to come.
<v Maritza Arroyo>我知道这会发生。这就是我不想来这里的原因。这就是我不想来的原因。

00:57:55.270 --> 00:57:58.610
<v Meema Spadola>You've got the biggest smile on your face. You look so happy right now.
<v Meema Spadola>你的脸上带着最大的微笑。你现在看起来太快乐了。

00:57:58.610 --> 00:58:22.720
<v Maritza Arroyo>Because I love boxing, that's why. It's got me where I'm at today, OK, very happy and very balanced, I guess. We're around Second Avenue, Second Avenue, between Second and Third, and 13th Street. So here I am, with no voice, going in this room to go spar. Is that crazy? That's crazy?
<v Maritza Arroyo>因为我热爱拳击，这就是原因。它让我今天在这里，好吗，非常快乐和平衡，我猜。我们在第二大道，第二大道，在第二和第三街之间，第13街。所以我在，没有声音，走进这个房间去陪练。那疯狂吗？那疯狂吗？

00:58:22.720 --> 00:58:35.500
<v Meema Spadola>She grabs her bag, and we race back to the gym. And as Maritza's getting dressed, I notice she wears tiny golden gloves on a chain around her neck. Milton stands ringside, pumped up, ready to see his favorite in action again.
<v Meema Spadola>她抓起她的包，我们赛车回到健身房。当玛丽扎正在穿衣服时，我注意到她脖子上带着一串细小的金手套项链。米尔顿站在场边，充满能量，准备再次看到他最爱的人行动。

00:58:35.500 --> 00:58:40.860
<v Howard Kelso>This is Howard Kelso live, right here from Supreme Team Boxing.
<v Howard Kelso>这是霍华德·凯尔索现场直播，就在Supreme Team Boxing这里。

00:58:40.860 --> 00:58:42.820
<v Howard Kelso>[BEEPING]
<v Howard Kelso>[哔哔声]

00:58:42.820 --> 00:58:48.760
<v Man>Box.
<v Man>盒。

00:58:48.760 --> 00:58:54.740
<v Milton>Relax your shoulders, Maritza. Relax your shoulders. Too tight. Ooh, good one.
<v Milton>放松你的肩膀，玛丽扎。放松你的肩膀。太紧了。噢，好的一拳。

00:58:54.740 --> 00:59:11.310
<v Meema Spadola>Maritza's stiff at first, then she starts to relax. She's ducking down, dancing around the ring. And in the last 10 seconds of the fight, she has a surge of energy. She's punching hard, moving fast, throwing nonstop combinations.
<v Meema Spadola>玛丽扎起初很僵硬，然后她开始放松。她低头躲避，在拳击场上跳舞。在比赛的最后10秒，她能量暴涨。她出拳有力，移动快速，不停地扔出组合拳。

00:59:11.310 --> 00:59:15.710
<v Milton>Come on, girl.
<v Milton>来吧，女孩。

00:59:15.710 --> 00:59:16.660
<v Milton>[BEEPING]
<v Milton>[哔哔声]

00:59:16.660 --> 00:59:19.030
<v Milton>Time.
<v Milton>时间。

00:59:19.030 --> 00:59:45.000
<v Meema Spadola>And afterwards, she's pumped up with adrenaline, sweating, laughing with Milton and the guys in the gym. She says she'll be back to spar and train every week. And even though she's missed the deadline for this year's Golden Gloves, she swears she'll take the gloves next year. Stay tuned for 1999, she says. Stay tuned.
<v Meema Spadola>之后，她充满了肾上腺素，流着汗，和米尔顿以及健身房里的伙计们笑着。她说她每周都会回来陪练和训练。即使她错过了今年金手套比赛的截止日期，她发誓明年会拿到手套。明年见，她说。明年见。

00:59:45.000 --> 00:59:59.020
<v Meema Spadola>But Maritza doesn't show at Milton's the next week or the week after. She breaks two appointments with me. She doesn't return my calls. And when I finally reach her, she's angry-- angry she fought again, scared she's getting sucked back in.
<v Meema Spadola>但玛丽扎下周或下下周没出现在米尔顿的健身房。她和我取消了两次约会。她没回我的电话。当我最终联系上她时，她很生气——生气她又打了架，害怕她被吸回去。

00:59:59.020 --> 01:00:05.320
<v Meema Spadola>And how about the fact that you're still carrying around your gear?
<v Meema Spadola>而且你一直带着你的装备的事实怎么样？

01:00:05.320 --> 01:00:29.270
<v Maritza Arroyo>Well, I guess I can't let go of boxing yet. Maybe it's my security blanket. It's like always knowing that it's always there, that I can always hit that bag. I get in front of the mirror at my house every day, just jab and come around, and do the moves.
<v Maritza Arroyo>好吧，我猜我还不能放弃拳击。也许它是我的安全毯。就像总是知道它总是在那里，我总能击中那个袋子。我每天在房子的镜子前，只是刺拳然后绕过来，做动作。

01:00:29.270 --> 01:00:47.600
<v Maritza Arroyo>It's my connection to boxing. I carry this with me. I sleep with it. I have gloves in my car. I love it. It's me.
<v Maritza Arroyo>这是我和拳击的联系。我带着这个。我带着它睡觉。我的车里有手套。我爱它。这是我。

01:00:47.600 --> 01:01:23.210
<v Ira Glass>That story from Meema Spadola. Maritza has stopped boxing herself. She's aged out of it. These days, she teaches people to box.
<v Ira Glass>那个故事来自米玛·斯帕多拉。玛丽扎自己停止了拳击。她年纪大了，离开了。这些天，她教别人拳击。

